# The codemap merge driver used to live here, resolving INDEX.md and
# FEATURES.md by regenerating them from the merged tree. It is gone because
# the files are gone from the repository (2026-08-08, Q54): they are derived
# artefacts the session hook and CI rebuild on demand, and committing them
# made every pair of parallel branches conflict by construction — on GitHub,
# where no merge driver ever runs, that meant every open pull request went
# red the moment any other one merged.
#
# The temptation this file used to warn about still stands, one step over:
# do NOT add a merge driver (or union attribute) for the ledgers. BUGS.md,
# ROADMAP.md, QUESTIONS.md and MANUAL.md are authored prose a script cannot
# reproduce — `bugs.py sync` rewrites checkboxes in them, it cannot rewrite
# the entries. Two branches that each filed a bug have two entries that both
# have to survive, and which id each keeps is a judgement. Auto-resolving
# that throws away work while reporting success. The pre-push `bugs.py ids`
# gate is what guards them instead.
